NAME: Reactivation batch
OWNER: CRM & Reactivation
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every Wednesday at 7:53 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Reactivation batch" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Reactivation batch · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state and data only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files. Items you queue for the owner still go in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/<your slug>/, with ids starting test-, and are never sent.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Reactivation batch · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Reactivation batch · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Reactivation batch · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Reactivation batch · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

Stop exception: if the stop file exists, the stop check above applies in full except for one action it doesn't forbid because it only removes a send: before you end the run, unschedule every REACT- email you scheduled that hasn't sent yet, and list in the daily note anything you couldn't unschedule.
First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/crm-reactivation/ with an id starting react- (or test-react-) that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-crm-reactivation.md yet, act on it with the reactivation-batch skill (quote follow-up decisions, ids starting qq-, belong to the quiet-quote-followup skill and the CRM sweep routine, not here). A yes is acted on only after the send gate in the skill passes: stop file absent, not test mode and config.json run is tommy, live_sends true, the hash recomputed from the pending item's payload matching the decision's, and the id not in the sent keys. Then create the HubSpot list and marketing email once, as approved. A no is recorded as declined and a change is redrafted once as a new item; add every handled id and its outcome to the sent keys. TMEC Command may already have nudged you to do this in your own chat; this is the fallback. In test mode (this routine is listed test, or config.json run is test), never create or send anything and make no treg call: write what you would have done to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, start item ids with test-, and say "not verified: test".
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-crm-reactivation/ and do it first.
Then use the reactivation-batch skill: if no batch is waiting on Tommy and the cadence says one is due, pick the people, verify their emails with treg (no treg call in test mode), draft the email and the text message, and put the batch in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/crm-reactivation/ as one item in the item format (a payload with TO as the list file's path, sha256 and count, the SEND time, the subject and the exact text, then the HASH), with how the list was picked in WHY. Never send, schedule or create anything in HubSpot in this step. If a batch is already waiting, or none is due, or no one passes the gates, write NO_CHANGE and stop.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/crm-reactivation.md (if the CRM sweep already wrote it today, append a section and never overwrite it): the last batch's results (HubSpot's own numbers, labelled as HubSpot's), opt-outs seen, the new batch waiting (counts and how picked, no addresses), anything blocked and why.
